  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Start Ready - Senegal Drought response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to lessen the immediate effects of drought on agropastoral households in Ran&#xe9;rou and Kanel and prevent worsening nutrition. It focuses on two main actions: providing anticipatory cash assistance to vulnerable families to meet essential food needs and avoid harmful coping strategies, and protecting the nutrition of young children and pregnant or breastfeeding women through community malnutrition screening, improved referrals, and promotion of good feeding practices. Targeting the areas hit hardest by low rainfall, the project relies on strong community engagement and local coordination to deliver a rapid, integrated response. Overall, it seeks to reduce livelihood losses, prevent acute malnutrition, and strengthen household resilience before the next lean season.</narrative>
  </description>
